hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1109","Chapter on the inviolability of the blood of covenanted non-Muslims, 1148 - Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, he said: Yazid, meaning Ibn Harun, narrated to us, he said: Uyaynah, meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman, informed us, from his father, from Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills a covenanted person unlawfully, Allah forbids him Paradise, even to smell its fragrance."
